# Contributing to {{ project_name }}

## Workflow: GitHub Flow

1. `main` is always releasable and protected: no direct pushes.
2. Branch from the latest `main`: `git switch -c <type>/<short-description>` (e.g. `feat/csv-export`, `fix/null-pointer`).
3. Commit small, logical steps. Rebase on `main` to stay current: `git fetch && git rebase origin/main`.
4. Open a pull request. CI must pass.
5. **Squash-merge.** The PR title becomes the single commit on `main`, so it must be a Conventional Commit.

## Commit messages: Conventional Commits

```
<type>(<optional scope>): <imperative summary, ≤72 chars>

<optional body: what and why, not how>

<optional footer: BREAKING CHANGE: ..., Refs: #123>
```

| Type | Use for | Version bump |
|---|---|---|
| `feat` | New user-facing capability | minor |
| `fix` | Bug fix | patch |
| `docs`, `style`, `refactor`, `perf`, `test`, `build`, `ci`, `chore` | Everything else | none |
| `feat!` / `BREAKING CHANGE:` footer | Incompatible change | major |

The `commit-msg` hook rejects messages that don't match.

## Local setup

```bash
pre-commit install   # once per clone
```

All commits must be signed.
